[2026-09-16T15:43:10] Q098: What can you tell me about the film King Kong?
{"id": "Q098", "question": "What can you tell me about the film King Kong?", "information_need": "overview", "motivation": "bored_random", "prior_familiarity": "unfamiliar", "scope": "multi_document", "answerable": true, "adversarial_kind": "ambiguous_entity", "required_sources": ["King_Kong_(1976_film).html", "78th_Academy_Awards.html"], "expected_sources": ["King_Kong_(1976_film).html", "78th_Academy_Awards.html"], "retrieved_sources": ["King_Kong_(1976_film).html", "Brokeback_Mountain.html", "The_Wings_of_the_Dove_(1997_film).html"], "required_aspects": ["The corpus covers more than one.", "The 1976 King Kong, directed by John Guillermin and produced by Dino De Laurentiis, starred Jeff Bridges, Charles Grodin and Jessica Lange", "it won a Special Achievement Academy Award for Visual Effects and was nominated for Best Cinematography and Best Sound.", "Separately, a King Kong film was among the multiple-award winners at the 78th Academy Awards, taking three awards alongside Brokeback Mountain, Crash and Memoirs of a Geisha.", "Please specify which you mean."], "response": "King Kong is a 1976 American adventure monster film directed by John Guillermin and written by Lorenzo Semple Jr. It stars Jeff Bridges, Charles Grodin, and Jessica Lange, and was produced by Dino De Laurentiis and distributed by Paramount Pictures. [King_Kong_(1976_film).html]\n\nIt is a remake of the 1933 film about “a giant ape who is captured and taken to New York City for exhibition,” and it is described as the fifth entry in the King Kong franchise. [King_Kong_(1976_film).html]\n\nThe film runs 134 minutes, is in English, and was made in the United States and Italy. Its budget was $23–24 million, and it grossed about $90.6 million. [King_Kong_(1976_film).html]\n\nIt was released on December 17, 1976, received mixed reviews, and won a Special Achievement Academy Award for Best Visual Effects. It was also nominated for Best Cinematography and Best Sound. [King_Kong_(1976_film).html]\n\nThe plot follows an expedition to a hidden island where the team discovers Kong, who is taken to New York City and later dies after climbing the World Trade Center and being attacked by the military. [King_Kong_(1976_film).html]", "closed_book_response": "**King Kong** is a famous monster/adventure story that has been adapted into several films over the years. The original and most iconic version is the **1933 film**, directed by **Merian C. Cooper and Ernest B. Schoedsack**.\n\n### Basic story\nThe plot usually centers on a giant ape, **Kong**, who lives on a mysterious island. A film crew or expedition discovers him, captures him, and brings him to civilization, where he escapes and causes chaos. At the heart of the story is also a tragic relationship between Kong and a human woman, usually **Ann Darrow**.\n\n### Why it’s important\n- It’s considered a landmark in **special effects** and **stop-motion animation**.\n- The original film was especially influential in shaping the **monster movie** genre.\n- Kong is one of the most enduring figures in popular culture, appearing in many remakes and reimaginings.\n\n### Notable versions\n- **1933**: The original classic\n- **1976**: A modernized remake\n- **2005**: Directed by **Peter Jackson**\n- There have also been crossover films, such as those in the broader **MonsterVerse** series\n\n### Themes\nThe film often explores:\n- Beauty and the beast-style tragedy\n- Humanity’s exploitation of nature\n- The consequences of greed and spectacle\n- Sympathy for the “monster”\n\nIf you want, I can also give you:\n1. a plot summary of a specific version,\n2. a list of major King Kong films, or\n3. details about the 1933 original and its special effects.", "correctness": "pass", "graded_correctness": "complete", "graded_correctness_score": 1.0, "covered_aspects": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], "aspect_coverage": 1.0, "answer_relevance": "pass", "claims": [{"text": "King Kong is a 1976 American adventure monster film directed by John Guillermin and written by Lorenzo Semple Jr.", "cited_source": "King_Kong_(1976_film).html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "It stars Jeff Bridges, Charles Grodin, and Jessica Lange.", "cited_source": "King_Kong_(1976_film).html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "It was produced by Dino De Laurentiis and distributed by Paramount Pictures.", "cited_source": "King_Kong_(1976_film).html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "It is a remake of the 1933 film about a giant ape who is captured and taken to New York City for exhibition.", "cited_source": "King_Kong_(1976_film).html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "It is described as the fifth entry in the King Kong franchise.", "cited_source": "King_Kong_(1976_film).html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "The film runs 134 minutes.", "cited_source": "King_Kong_(1976_film).html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "It is in English.", "cited_source": "King_Kong_(1976_film).html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "It was made in the United States and Italy.", "cited_source": "King_Kong_(1976_film).html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "Its budget was $23–24 million.", "cited_source": "King_Kong_(1976_film).html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "It grossed about $90.6 million.", "cited_source": "King_Kong_(1976_film).html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "It was released on December 17, 1976.", "cited_source": "King_Kong_(1976_film).html", "grounded": true