{"id": "Q091", "question": "Tell me about Ben Kingsley's career — I know him from the Marvel films.", "information_need": "overview", "motivation": "media_reference", "prior_familiarity": "unfamiliar", "scope": "single_document", "answerable": true, "adversarial_kind": null, "required_sources": ["Ben_Kingsley.html"], "expected_sources": ["Ben_Kingsley.html"], "retrieved_sources": ["Ben_Kingsley.html", "Michael_B._Jordan.html", "Brendan_Fraser.html"], "required_aspects": ["Ben Kingsley (born Krishna Pandit Bhanji, 1943) began in theatre, joining the Royal Shakespeare Company in 1967 and working mainly on stage for 15 years.", "His film breakthrough was the title role in Richard Attenborough's Gandhi (1982), for which he won the Academy Award for Best Actor and the BAFTA for Best Actor in a Leading Role.", "He was Oscar-nominated for Bugsy (1990), Sexy Beast (2000) and House of Sand and Fog (2003), and was BAFTA-nominated for Schindler's List (1993).", "In the Marvel Cinematic Universe he has played Trevor Slattery for over a decade, in Iron Man 3 (2013), the short All Hail the King (2014), Shang-Chi and the Legend of the Ten Rings (2021) and the Disney+ series Wonder Man.", "He was appointed Knight Bachelor in 2002."], "response": "Ben Kingsley is a British-Indian actor whose career spans seven decades, with work in theatre, television, film, and voice roles [Ben_Kingsley.html]. He began in theatre, joining the Royal Shakespeare Company in 1967 and spending the next 15 years mainly on stage [Ben_Kingsley.html]. His stage work included *As You Like It*, *Much Ado About Nothing*, *Richard III*, *The Tempest*, *A Midsummer Night's Dream*, *Hamlet*, and *The Merry Wives of Windsor* [Ben_Kingsley.html].\n\nIn film, his defining role is Mahatma Gandhi in *Gandhi* (1982), for which he won the Academy Award for Best Actor and the BAFTA Award for Best Actor in a Leading Role [Ben_Kingsley.html]. He was later Oscar-nominated for *Bugsy* (1990), *Sexy Beast* (2000), and *House 