{"id": "Q006", "question": "Compare how the Academy handled the introduction of the Best Animated Feature category with the way the Best Original Score category was split and then merged again in the 1990s.", "information_need": "in_depth", "motivation": "work_or_school", "prior_familiarity": "familiar", "scope": "multi_document", "answerable": true, "adversarial_kind": null, "required_sources": ["74th_Academy_Awards.html", "68th_Academy_Awards.html"], "expected_sources": ["74th_Academy_Awards.html", "68th_Academy_Awards.html", "Academy_Award_for_Best_Animated_Feature.html"], "retrieved_sources": ["Academy_Award_for_Best_Director.html", "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "Academy_Award_for_Best_Production_Design.html"], "required_aspects": ["The Best Animated Feature award was introduced at the 74th ceremony (2002) as a brand-new competitive category with eligibility rules: at least 70 minutes long, a significant number of animated characters, and at least 75 percent animation", "a minimum of eight qualifying films had to be released in the year to allow three nominees, rising to five nominees if more than twelve films qualified.", "Before this, animated features such as Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs, Who Framed Roger Rabbit and Toy Story had only received Special Achievement Awards.", "By contrast, the score category was not created but divided: beginning with the 68th ceremony (1996) the music branch split Best Original Score into Best Dramatic Score and Best Musical or Comedy Score, seen as a response to Disney's dominance of the score and song categories", "four years later the two scoring categories were merged back into one."], "response": "The documents only explain the introduction of the Best Animated Feature category, not the Best Original Score category’s split-and-merge history. They say Best Animated Feature was created “for the 74th Academy Awards to ensure the recognition of animated films” and that, before its creation, “the only animated film ever nominated for Best Picture was 1991's Beauty and the Beast” [Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html]. They also note that “the Academy rules allow for a film to be nominated in both categories” [Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html].\n\nI do not have enough information in the provided documents to compare that with how Best Original Score was split and then merged again in the 1990s.", "closed_book_response": "The Academy handled the two situations quite differently:\n\n- **Best Animated Feature** was introduced as a **new permanent category** in 2001 (for films released in 2001 and awarded in 2002). It was created because animated films had become more prominent and the Academy wanted a dedicated competitive space for them. Once added, it stayed as its own separate award category.\n\n- **Best Original Score** was handled more like an **experimental category adjustment**. In the 1990s, the Academy **split** the music award into separate categories for **dramatic scores** and **musical scores** for a short period, but that arrangement proved awkward and was later **merged back into a single Best Original Score category**. So unlike Animated Feature, which was a lasting addition, the score change was temporary and then reversed.\n\nIn short: **Animated Feature was a new category that stuck; Original Score was divided temporarily and then recombined.**", "correctness": "fail", "graded_correctness": "incorrect", "graded_correctness_score": 0.0, "covered_aspects": [1, 3, 4, 5], "aspect_coverage": 0.8, "answer_relevance": "pass", "claims": [{"text": "The documents only explain the introduction of the Best Animated Feature category, not the Best Original Score category’s split-and-merge history.", "cited_source": null, "grounded": false, "citation_supported": null, "attributable_to_retrieval": null}, {"text": "Best Animated Feature was created “for the 74th Academy Awards to ensure the recognition of animated films.”", "cited_source": "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "Before Best Animated Feature was created, “the only animated film ever nominated for Best Picture was 1991's Beauty and the Beast.”", "cited_source": "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "The Academy rules allow for a film to be nominated in both Best Animated Feature and Best Picture categories.", "cited_source": "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "The speaker does not have enough information in the provided documents to compare that with how Best Original Score was split and then merged again in the 1990s.", "cited_source": null, "grounded": false, "citation_supported": null, "attributable_to_retrieval": null}], "claim_count": 5, "graded_groundedness_score": 0.6, "faithfulness": "fail", "citation_support_rate": 1.0, "chunk_attribution_score": 1.0, "source_hit_at_k": 0, "source_recall_at_k": 0.0, "source_precision_at_k": 0.0, "source_recall_strict": 0.0, "all_required_present": false, "response_quote_count": 3, "quote_fidelity_rate": 1.0, "quote_attribution_accuracy": 0.3333333333333333, "citation_count": 1, "citation_precision": 0.0, "unsupported_citation_rate": 0.0, "refusal_outcome": "n/a", "answer_latency_seconds": 4.583837999991374, "judge_latency_seconds": 4.747354299994186, "total_latency_seconds": 11.690229899977567, "input_tokens": 122218, "output_tokens": 702, "total_tokens": 122920, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.0948225}
