[2026-09-16T15:44:44] Q045: Compare the audience reactions and awards outcomes for the two films that lost Best Picture in the most talked-about upsets — the 2005 gay romance and the 2016 musical.
{"id": "Q045", "question": "Compare the audience reactions and awards outcomes for the two films that lost Best Picture in the most talked-about upsets — the 2005 gay romance and the 2016 musical.", "information_need": "in_depth", "motivation": "personal_decision", "prior_familiarity": "familiar", "scope": "multi_document", "answerable": true, "adversarial_kind": null, "required_sources": ["Brokeback_Mountain.html", "89th_Academy_Awards.html"], "expected_sources": ["Brokeback_Mountain.html", "89th_Academy_Awards.html", "La_La_Land.html", "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html"], "retrieved_sources": ["Brokeback_Mountain.html", "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "Gus_Van_Sant.html"], "required_aspects": ["Brokeback Mountain won three Academy Awards — Best Director, Best Adapted Screenplay and Best Original Score — but lost Best Picture to Crash, prompting accusations of homophobia and more than 800 supporters raising up to $26,000 for an advert in Daily Variety thanking the filmmakers.", "La La Land won six Oscars including Best Director and Best Actress from a record-tying fourteen nominations, but lost Best Picture to Moonlight after the envelope error, setting a record for most nominations without winning Best Picture.", "Both are considered landmark losses, and in a 2015 Hollywood Reporter member poll Brokeback Mountain won the revote for Best Picture."], "response": "The 2005 gay romance was **Brokeback Mountain**. Its loss to *Crash* for Best Picture was “heavily criticized,” with some critics accusing the Academy of homophobia, and presenter Jack Nicholson was caught mouthing “whoa” in surprise at the result. [Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html] It still had strong awards success overall: it won Best Director, Best Adapted Screenplay, and Original Score at the 78th Academy Awards, and also won major Golden Globe and BAFTA prizes. [Brokeback_Mountain.html]\n\nThe 2016 musical was **La La Land**. It received the famous Best Picture mix-up at the 89th Academy Awards, when it was mistakenly announced as the winner before *Moonlight* was revealed to have won instead. [Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html] The document does not describe the audience reaction to that upset in the same way it does for *Brokeback Mountain*, but it does confirm that *La La Land* did not ultimately win Best Picture. [Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html]\n\nSo, compared with *Brokeback Mountain*, which faced intense backlash over its Best Picture loss but had a strong haul of awards, *La La Land* was involved in an announcement error and did not get the Best Picture win, with no comparable audience-reaction detail provided in the documents. [Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html] [Brokeback_Mountain.html]", "closed_book_response": "The two films are **Brokeback Mountain** (2005) and **La La Land** (2016).\n\n### Audience reactions\n- **Brokeback Mountain** was generally seen as a major cultural landmark. It earned strong critical praise, lots of emotional engagement from audiences, and was widely discussed for its gay love story and its significance in mainstream cinema. The reaction was intense and respectful, though some backlash existed because of its subject matter.\n- **La La Land** had a more broadly enthusiastic, celebratory audience response. People loved its energy, music, style, and old-Hollywood charm. It was a crowd-pleaser and became a pop-culture favorite, especially with awards-season buzz.\n\n### Awards outcomes\n- **Brokeback Mountain** won several major awards, including **Best Director** at the Oscars, but it **lost Best Picture** to *Crash* in a result often viewed as one of the biggest upsets in Academy history.\n- **La La Land** won many awards too, including **Best Director**, but it also **lost Best Picture**—famously and mistakenly announced at first as the winner before *Moonlight* was corrected as the actual winner. That made it one of the most dramatic Oscar moments ever.\n\n### In short\n- **Brokeback Mountain**: emotionally powerful, groundbreaking, widely admired; lost Best Picture in a controversial upset.\n- **La La Land**: hugely popular, dreamy crowd-pleaser; lost Best Picture in an infamous live-telecast mix-up and upset.\n\nIf you want, I can also compare **why** each loss felt so shocking to viewers and voters.", "correctness": "pass", "graded_correctness": "substantially_complete", "graded_correctness_score": 0.75, "covered_aspects": [1, 2, 3], "aspect_coverage": 1.0, "answer_relevance": "pass", "claims": [{"text": "The 2005 gay romance was Brokeback Mountain.", "cited_source": "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": false, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "Its loss to Crash for Best Picture was heavily criticized.", "cited_source": "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "Some critics accused the Academy of homophobia over that loss.", "cited_source": "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "Presenter Jack Nicholson was caught mouthing 'whoa' in surprise at the result.", "cited_source": "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "Brokeback Mountain won Best Director at the 78th Academy Awards.", "cited_source": "Brokeback_Mountain.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "Brokeback Mountain won Best Adapted Screenplay at the 78th Academy Awards.", "cited_source": "Brokeback_Mountain.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "Brokeback Mountain won Original Score at the 78th Academy Awards.", "cited_source": "Brokeback_Mountain.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "Brokeback Mountain also won major Golden Globe prizes.", "cited_source": "Brokeback_Mountain.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "Brokeback Mountain also won major BAFTA prizes.", "cited_source": "Brokeback_Mountain.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "The 2016 musical was La La Land.", "cited_source": null, "grounded": true, "citation_supported": null, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "La La Land had a Best Picture mix-up at the 89th Academy Awards.", "cited_source": "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "La La Land was mistakenly announced as the winner before Moonlight was revealed to have won instead.", "cited_source": "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "The document does not describe the audience reaction to that upset in the same way it does for Brokeback Mountain.", "cited_source": "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "grounded": false, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": null}, {"text": "The documents confirm that La La Land did not ultimately win Best Picture.", "cited_source": "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "Compared with Brokeback Mountain, La La Land was involved in an announcement error.", "cited_source": "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "Compared with Brokeback Mountain, La La Land did not get the Best Picture win.", "cited_source": "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "No comparable audience-reaction detail is provided for La La Land in the documents.", "cited_source": "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "grounded": false, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": null}], "claim_count": 17, "graded_groundedness_score": 0.8823529411764706, "faithfulness": "fail", "citation_support_rate": 0.9375, "chunk_attribution_score": 0.4666666666666667, "source_hit_at_k": 1, "source_recall_at_k": 0.5, "source_precision_at_k": 0.6666666666666666, "source_recall_strict": 0.0, "all_required_present": false, "response_quote_count": 1, "quote_fidelity_rate": 1.0, "quote_attribution_accuracy": 0.0, "citation_count": 2, "citation_precision": 1.0, "unsupported_citation_rate": 0.0, "refusal_outcome": "hallucinated", "answer_latency_seconds": 2.662390100012999, "judge_latency_seconds": 9.152510099986102, "total_latency_seconds": 14.723959900002228, "input_tokens": 155392, "output_tokens": 1579, "total_tokens": 156971, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.1236495}
