{"id": "Q067", "question": "What awards did Whiplash win at Sundance when it premiered, and how does that relate to the short film of the same name?", "information_need": "overview", "motivation": "work_or_school", "prior_familiarity": "familiar", "scope": "multi_document", "answerable": true, "adversarial_kind": null, "required_sources": ["Whiplash_(2014_film).html", "La_La_Land.html"], "expected_sources": ["Whiplash_(2014_film).html", "La_La_Land.html", "Damien_Chazelle.html"], "retrieved_sources": ["Whiplash_(2014_film).html", "La_La_Land.html", "Damien_Chazelle.html"], "required_aspects": ["The feature Whiplash premiered in competition at the 2014 Sundance Film Festival on January 16 as the festival's opening film and won both the Audience Award Dramatic and the Grand Jury Prize Dramatic.", "One year earlier, Chazelle's eighteen-minute short of the same name — made from fifteen pages of the feature script to attract investors — debuted at the 2013 festival and won the short film Jury Award for fiction.", "That earlier premiere later caused the Academy to classify the feature screenplay as adapted rather than original."], "response": "Whiplash premiered at the 2014 Sundance Film Festival, where it won the Audience Award Dramatic and the Grand Jury Prize Dramatic [Whiplash_(2014_film).html]. The film’s short-film predecessor of the same name had earlier won the short film Jury Award for fiction at the 2013 Sundance Film Festival [Whiplash_(2014_film).html].", "closed_book_response": "At Sundance, **Whiplash** won both:\n\n- the **Grand Jury Prize**  \n- the **Audience Award**\n\nfor the **U.S. Dramatic** category.\n\nAs for the short film of the same name: the feature-length *Whiplash* was **expanded from Damien Chazelle’s earlier short film, also titled *Whiplash***. The short served as the basis for the feature and helped Chazelle develop the story and prove the concept before making the full movie.", "correctness": "pass", "graded_correctness": "complete", "graded_correctness_score": 1.0, "covered_aspects": [1, 2, 3], "aspect_coverage": 1.0, "answer_relevance": "pass", "claims": [{"text": "Whiplash premiered at the 2014 Sundance Film Festival.", "cited_source": "Whiplash_(2014_film).html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "At that festival, Whiplash won the Audience Award Dramatic and the Grand Jury Prize Dramatic.", "cited_source": "Whiplash_(2014_film).html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "The short-film predecessor of Whiplash had the same name.", "cited_source": "Whiplash_(2014_film).html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "That short film had earlier won the short film Jury Award for fiction at the 2013 Sundance Film Festival.", "cited_source": "Whiplash_(2014_film).html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}], "claim_count": 4, "graded_groundedness_score": 1.0, "faithfulness": "pass", "citation_support_rate": 1.0, "chunk_attribution_score": 0.0, "source_hit_at_k": 1, "source_recall_at_k": 1.0, "source_precision_at_k": 1.0, "source_recall_strict": 1.0, "all_required_present": true, "response_quote_count": 0, "quote_fidelity_rate": null, "quote_attribution_accuracy": null, "citation_count": 1, "citation_precision": 1.0, "unsupported_citation_rate": 0.0, "refusal_outcome": "n/a", "answer_latency_seconds": 2.234671000012895, "judge_latency_seconds": 4.753300899988972, "total_latency_seconds": 8.96329740001238, "input_tokens": 131328, "output_tokens": 474, "total_tokens": 131802, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.100629}
