[2026-09-16T15:46:03] Q094: I'm deciding whether to watch a long Western — how does Costner's Horizon project compare in scale and reception to his earlier epic?
{"id": "Q094", "question": "I'm deciding whether to watch a long Western — how does Costner's Horizon project compare in scale and reception to his earlier epic?", "information_need": "in_depth", "motivation": "personal_decision", "prior_familiarity": "familiar", "scope": "multi_document", "answerable": true, "adversarial_kind": null, "required_sources": ["Kevin_Costner.html"], "expected_sources": ["Kevin_Costner.html", "Academy_Award_for_Best_Director.html"], "retrieved_sources": ["Kevin_Costner.html", "Titanic_(1997_film).html", "Steven_Spielberg.html"], "required_aspects": ["Horizon: An American Saga is a Western epic split into at least four films, each just under three hours long, with Costner both directing and starring", "production on the first film was expected to last at least 220 days.", "Chapter 1 was released in June 2024, earned mixed reviews and was a box office flop, which contributed to Chapter 2 being delayed indefinitely after debuting at the 81st Venice International Film Festival to similarly mixed reviews.", "By contrast, his earlier epic Dances With Wolves won him two Academy Awards, and his 2003 Western Open Range received critical acclaim and was a surprise commercial success."], "response": "Costner’s earlier epic was *Dances With Wolves*, which “was nominated for 12 Academy Awards and won seven, including two for him personally (Best Picture and Best Director)” [Kevin_Costner.html]. By contrast, *Horizon: An American Saga* is described as “a Western epic that will be split into at least four films, each just under three hours in length” [Kevin_Costner.html]. The first chapter, released in June 2024, “earned mixed reviews, and was a box office flop” [Kevin_Costner.html]. Its poor box-office returns contributed to the “indefinite delay of Chapter 2,” which also “had received mixed reviews” [Kevin_Costner.html].\n\nSo, in scale, *Horizon* is larger as a multi-film project; in reception, it has been far less warmly received than *Dances With Wolves* [Kevin_Costner.html].", "closed_book_response": "Kevin Costner’s **Horizon** project is broadly comparable to his earlier Western epic **Dances with Wolves** in ambition, but it’s larger in structure and much more uneven in reception.\n\n### Scale\n- **Dances with Wolves (1990)** was a single, self-contained epic film.\n- **Horizon** is conceived as a **multi-part saga**—a much bigger, serialized Western project spanning multiple chapters.\n- In terms of **scope**, Horizon is the more sprawling undertaking: more characters, multiple storylines, and a longer-form vision for the American West.\n\n### Reception\n- **Dances with Wolves** was a major critical and commercial triumph. It won **Best Picture** and helped define Costner’s reputation as a serious filmmaker.\n- **Horizon** has had a far more mixed and uncertain reception. It was widely seen as an ambitious passion project, but it did **not** launch with anything close to the same acclaim or universal enthusiasm.\n- Critics and audiences have been more divided on Horizon, with many praising the ambition and production values but questioning the pacing, structure, and whether the project’s size is paying off.\n\n### Bottom line\nIf you’re choosing based on **reputation and proven payoff**, **Dances with Wolves** is the safer bet: it’s a classic with a huge legacy.  \nIf you want **something more sprawling and possibly more “epic” in a modern, multipart sense**, **Horizon** is the bigger swing—but also the riskier one.\n\nIf you want, I can also compare them in terms of **runtime, tone, or how accessible they are for someone who isn’t a huge Western fan**.", "correctness": "pass", "graded_correctness": "complete", "graded_correctness_score": 1.0, "covered_aspects": [1, 3, 4], "aspect_coverage": 0.75, "answer_relevance": "pass", "claims": [{"text": "Costner’s earlier epic was *Dances With Wolves*.", "cited_source": "Kevin_Costner.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "*Dances With Wolves* was nominated for 12 Academy Awards and won seven.", "cited_source": "Kevin_Costner.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "*Dances With Wolves* won two Academy Awards for Costner personally: Best Picture and Best Director.", "cited_source": "Kevin_Costner.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "*Horizon: An American Saga* is a Western epic.", "cited_source": "Kevin_Costner.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "*Horizon: An American Saga* will be split into at least four films.", "cited_source": "Kevin_Costner.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "Each *Horizon* film is just under three hours in length.", "cited_source": "Kevin_Costner.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "The first chapter of *Horizon: An American Saga* was released in June 2024.", "cited_source": "Kevin_Costner.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "The first chapter of *Horizon* earned mixed reviews.", "cited_source": "Kevin_Costner.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "The first chapter of *Horizon* was a box office flop.", "cited_source": "Kevin_Costner.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "The poor box-office returns of Chapter 1 contributed to the indefinite delay of Chapter 2.", "cited_source": "Kevin_Costner.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "Chapter 2 had also received mixed reviews after its debut at the 81st Venice International Film Festival.", "cited_source": "Kevin_Costner.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "In scale, *Horizon* is larger as a multi-film project.", "cited_source": "Kevin_Costner.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": false, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "In reception, *Horizon* has been far less warmly received than *Dances With Wolves*.", "cited_source": "Kevin_Costner.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": false, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}], "claim_count": 13, "graded_groundedness_score": 1.0, "faithfulness": "pass", "citation_support_rate": 0.8461538461538461, "chunk_attribution_score": 0.15384615384615385, "source_hit_at_k": 1, "source_recall_at_k": 1.0, "source_precision_at_k": 0.3333333333333333, "source_recall_strict": 1.0, "all_required_present": true, "response_quote_count": 5, "quote_fidelity_rate": 0.8, "quote_attribution_accuracy": 0.6, "citation_count": 1, "citation_precision": 1.0, "unsupported_citation_rate": 0.0, "refusal_outcome": "n/a", "answer_latency_seconds": 3.5218025000067428, "judge_latency_seconds": 14.022336100024404, "total_latency_seconds": 20.701776900037657, "input_tokens": 346171, "output_tokens": 1227, "total_tokens": 347398, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.26514975}
