[2026-09-16T18:37:54] Q007: Comparing a 1950s motor-racing catastrophe in France to a 1960s Alaskan natural disaster, which killed more people, and what safety regulations followed each?
{"id": "Q007", "question": "Comparing a 1950s motor-racing catastrophe in France to a 1960s Alaskan natural disaster, which killed more people, and what safety regulations followed each?", "information_need": "in_depth", "motivation": "work_or_school", "prior_familiarity": "familiar", "scope": "multi_document", "answerable": true, "adversarial_kind": null, "required_sources": ["1955_Le_Mans_disaster.html", "1964_Alaska_earthquake.html"], "expected_sources": ["1955_Le_Mans_disaster.html", "1964_Alaska_earthquake.html"], "retrieved_sources": ["1955_Le_Mans_disaster.html", "History_of_Formula_One.html", "1964_Alaska_earthquake.html"], "required_aspects": ["The 1964 Alaska earthquake and its tsunamis killed 139 people, more than the 1955 Le Mans disaster's estimated 82 to 84 deaths.", "The Le Mans disaster led to temporary bans on motorsports in France, Spain, Switzerland, West Germany, and other nations until racetracks met higher safety standards.", "The Alaska earthquake led to the formation of the West Coast and Alaska Tsunami Warning Center as a direct response to the disaster."], "response": "The 1964 Alaska earthquake killed more people: 139 deaths, compared with at least 82 deaths in the 1955 Le Mans disaster.[1964_Alaska_earthquake.html][1955_Le_Mans_disaster.html]\n\nSafety changes followed both disasters. After Le Mans, the Circuit de la Sarthe was extensively improved: the pit straight was redesigned and widened to remove the kink and add a deceleration lane, the pits were rebuilt, and the grandstand was replaced with new spectator terraces separated from the track by a wide ditch.[1955_Le_Mans_disaster.html] The official inquiry also blamed the track’s inadequate safety standards rather than any specific driver.[1955_Le_Mans_disaster.html]\n\nAfter the Alaska earthquake, the West Coast and Alaska Tsunami Warning Center was formed directly in response, and the Alaska Division of Emergency Services was established by the Alaska National Guard for future disasters.[1964_Alaska_earthquake.html]", "closed_book_response": "The **1955 Le Mans disaster** in France killed **more people** than the **1964 Alaska earthquake**.\n\n- **1955 Le Mans disaster**: a racing crash caused debris to strike the crowd, killing **about 83 spectators and one driver** (often cited as **84 total**).  \n  - **Safety regulations that followed:** major changes to **motor-racing safety**, including stronger separation between track and spectators, improved crash protection, and stricter event safety standards. In some places, racing regulations became more cautious about circuit design, barriers, and crowd control.\n\n- **1964 Alaska earthquake**: this massive quake and resulting tsunami killed **about 131 people**.  \n  - **Safety regulations that followed:** the disaster led to major improvements in **earthquake-resistant building codes**, **tsunami warning systems**, and broader **seismic safety planning** in Alaska and the United States.\n\nSo, **the Alaska earthquake killed more people overall**, though the **Le Mans disaster led to major motor-sport safety reforms**.", "correctness": "fail", "graded_correctness": "substantially_complete", "graded_correctness_score": 0.75, "covered_aspects": [1, 2, 3], "aspect_coverage": 1.0, "answer_relevance": "pass", "claims": [{"text": "The 1964 Alaska earthquake killed 139 people.", "cited_source": "1964_Alaska_earthquake.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "The 1955 Le Mans disaster killed at least 82 people.", "cited_source": "1955_Le_Mans_disaster.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "Safety changes followed both disasters.", "cited_source": null, "grounded": true, "citation_supported": null, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "After Le Mans, the Circuit de la Sarthe was extensively improved.", "cited_source": "1955_Le_Mans_disaster.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "The pit straight was redesigned and widened to remove the kink.", "cited_source": "1955_Le_Mans_disaster.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "A deceleration lane was added.", "cited_source": "1955_Le_Mans_disaster.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "The pits were rebuilt.", "cited_source": "1955_Le_Mans_disaster.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "The grandstand was replaced with new spectator terraces separated from the track by a wide ditch.", "cited_source": "1955_Le_Mans_disaster.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "The official inquiry blamed the track’s inadequate safety standards rather than any specific driver.", "cited_source": "1955_Le_Mans_disaster.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "After the Alaska earthquake, the West Coast and Alaska Tsunami Warning Center was formed directly in response.", "cited_source": "1964_Alaska_earthquake.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "The Alaska Division of Emergency Services was established by the Alaska National Guard for future disasters.", "cited_source": "1964_Alaska_earthquake.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}], "claim_count": 11, "graded_groundedness_score": 1.0, "faithfulness": "pass", "citation_support_rate": 1.0, "chunk_attribution_score": 0.7272727272727273, "source_hit_at_k": 1, "source_recall_at_k": 1.0, "source_precision_at_k": 0.6666666666666666, "source_recall_strict": 1.0, "all_required_present": true, "response_quote_count": 0, "quote_fidelity_rate": null, "quote_attribution_accuracy": null, "citation_count": 2, "citatio