[2026-09-16T19:02:37] Q098: What can you tell me about the film King Kong?
{"id": "Q098", "question": "What can you tell me about the film King Kong?", "information_need": "overview", "motivation": "bored_random", "prior_familiarity": "unfamiliar", "scope": "multi_document", "answerable": true, "adversarial_kind": "ambiguous_entity", "required_sources": ["King_Kong_(1976_film).html", "King_Kong_(2005_film).html"], "expected_sources": ["King_Kong_(1976_film).html", "King_Kong_(2005_film).html", "78th_Academy_Awards.html", "King_Kong_(franchise).html"], "retrieved_sources": ["Godzilla_(1998_film).html", "King_Kong_(2005_film).html", "Brokeback_Mountain.html"], "required_aspects": ["The corpus covers more than one.", "The 1976 King Kong, directed by John Guillermin and produced by Dino De Laurentiis, starred Jeff Bridges, Charles Grodin and Jessica Lange; it won a Special Achievement Academy Award for Visual Effects and was nominated for Best Cinematography and Best Sound.", "The 2005 King Kong, directed by Peter Jackson, won three Academy Awards at the 78th ceremony — Best Sound Editing, Best Sound Mixing and Best Visual Effects.", "Please specify which you mean."], "response": "King Kong is a 2005 epic monster film directed, co-written, and produced by Peter Jackson. It stars Naomi Watts, Jack Black, Adrien Brody, Thomas Kretschmann, Colin Hanks, Jamie Bell, and Andy Serkis as Kong via motion capture. [King_Kong_(2005_film).html]\n\nThe film is the ninth entry in the King Kong franchise and the second remake of the 1933 film. It was set in 1933 and follows a filmmaker’s expedition to Skull Island, where the crew encounters Kong and other prehistoric creatures. [King_Kong_(2005_film).html]\n\nIt had a budget of $207 million and grossed $556.9 million at the box office. It ran for 187 minutes and was released by Universal Pictures. [King_Kong_(2005_film).html]\n\nThe film received critical acclaim, with praise for its special effects, performances, and spectacle, and it won three Academy Awards for Best Sound Editing, Best Sound Mixing, and Best Visual Effects. [King_Kong_(2005_film).html]", "closed_book_response": "**King Kong** is a famous giant-monster adventure film that first appeared in **1933**. It’s one of the most influential movies ever made, especially in the fantasy and special-effects genres.\n\n### Basic idea\nThe story usually follows a filmmaker or expedition crew that travels to a mysterious island and discovers **King Kong**, a gigantic ape. Kong is captured and brought to civilization, where he escapes and causes chaos, often driven by his attachment to a human woman.\n\n### Why it matters\n- It was groundbreaking for its **special effects** at the time, especially stop-motion animation.\n- It became a major cultural icon and helped define the “giant monster” movie.\n- The image of Kong climbing a skyscraper is one of the most famous scenes in movie history.\n\n### Main versions\nThere have been several film versions and remakes, including:\n- **1933 original**\n- **1976** remake\n- **2005** version directed by **Peter Jackson**\n- **2017’s Kong: Skull Island**, which is part of a shared monster universe\n\n### Themes\nCommon themes include:\n- beauty and the beast\n- nature versus civilization\n- exploitation and captivity\n- tragedy in the relationship between humans and the monster\n\nIf you want, I can also give you:\n- a plot summary of the **1933 original**\n- a comparison of the different remakes\n- or a list of the main cast and crew for a specific version", "correctness": "fail", "graded_correctness": "incorrect", "graded_correctness_score": 0.0, "covered_aspects": [3], "aspect_coverage": 0.25, "answer_relevance": "pass", "claims": [{"text": "King Kong is a 2005 epic monster film directed, co-written, and produced by Peter Jackson.", "cited_source": "King_Kong_(2005_film).html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "It stars Naomi Watts, Jack Black, Adrien Brody, Thomas Kretschmann, Colin Hanks, Jamie Bell, and Andy Serki