[2026-09-16T19:03:04] Q091: Tell me about Ben Kingsley's career — I know him from the Marvel films.
{"id": "Q091", "question": "Tell me about Ben Kingsley's career — I know him from the Marvel films.", "information_need": "overview", "motivation": "media_reference", "prior_familiarity": "unfamiliar", "scope": "single_document", "answerable": true, "adversarial_kind": null, "required_sources": ["Ben_Kingsley.html"], "expected_sources": ["Ben_Kingsley.html"], "retrieved_sources": ["Ben_Kingsley.html", "Schindler_s_List.html", "Chris_Columbus_(filmmaker).html"], "required_aspects": ["Ben Kingsley (born Krishna Pandit Bhanji, 1943) began in theatre, joining the Royal Shakespeare Company in 1967 and working mainly on stage for 15 years.", "His film breakthrough was the title role in Richard Attenborough's Gandhi (1982), for which he won the Academy Award for Best Actor and the BAFTA for Best Actor in a Leading Role.", "He was Oscar-nominated for Bugsy (1990), Sexy Beast (2000) and House of Sand and Fog (2003), and was BAFTA-nominated for Schindler's List (1993).", "In the Marvel Cinematic Universe he has played Trevor Slattery for over a decade, in Iron Man 3 (2013), the short All Hail the King (2014), Shang-Chi and the Legend of the Ten Rings (2021) and the Disney+ series Wonder Man.", "He was appointed Knight Bachelor in 2002."], "response": "Ben Kingsley is a British-Indian actor whose career began in theatre. He joined the Royal Shakespeare Company in 1967 and spent the next 15 years appearing mainly on stage, with productions including *As You Like It*, *Much Ado About Nothing*, *Richard III*, *The Tempest*, *A Midsummer Night's Dream*, *Hamlet* and *The Merry Wives of Windsor* [Ben_Kingsley.html].\n\nHe moved into film with a feature debut in *Fear Is the Key* (1972), and later became widely known for playing Mahatma Gandhi in *Gandhi* (1982), which won him the Academy Award for Best Actor and the BAFTA Award for Best Actor in a Leading Role [Ben_Kingsley.html]. Other notable films listed include *Maurice*, *Bugsy*, *Schindler's List*, *Sexy Beast*, *House of Sand and Fog*, *Shutter Island*, and *Hugo* [Ben_Kingsley.html]. For *Schindler's List*, he played Itzhak Stern [Schindler_s_List.html].\n\nSince you know him from Marvel: Kingsley played Trevor Slattery in the Marvel Cinematic Universe, appearing in *Iron Man 3* (2013), the short film *All Hail the King* (2014), *Shang-Chi and the Legend of the Ten Rings* (2021), and the Disney+ series *Wonder Man* (2026–present) [Ben_Kingsley.html].\n\nHe has also done voice work, including *The Jungle Book* (2016) and *The Boxtrolls* (2014) [Ben_Kingsley.html].", "closed_book_response": "Ben Kingsley is a highly respected British actor with a long career in film, television, and theater. He’s probably best known to many modern audiences as **Trevor Slattery** in the Marvel films, especially **Iron Man 3**, where he plays the actor posing as the Mandarin. He later returned to the role in **Shang-Chi and the Legend of the Ten Rings**.\n\nBut his career goes far beyond Marvel. Some key points:\n\n- **Breakout role:** He became internationally famous for playing **Mohandas Gandhi** in **Gandhi (1982)**. That performance won him the **Academy Award for Best Actor**.\n- **Range of roles:** He’s played a wide variety of characters — historical figures, villains, heroes, and supporting roles in major studio films.\n- **Notable films:** He has appeared in movies such as **Schindler’s List**, **Sexy Beast**, **House of Sand and Fog**, **Hugo**, **The Physician**, and **Shutter Island**.\n- **Style:** Kingsley is known for being intense, controlled, and very adaptable, often bringing precision and depth to morally complex characters.\n- **Recognition:** Beyond his Oscar, he has received many other honors and was knighted in the UK, becoming **Sir Ben Kingsley**.\n\nIn short, while Marvel introduced him to a newer generation, Ben Kingsley was already an acclaimed major actor long before that. If you want, I can also give you a “best performances” watch list for him.", "correctness": "pass", "graded_correctness": "complete", "graded_correctness_score": 1.0, "covered_aspects": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], "aspect_coverage": 1.0, "answer_relevance": "pass", "claims": [{"text": "Ben Kingsley is a British-Indian actor.", "cited_source": "Ben_Kingsley.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "His career began in theatre.", "cited_source": "Ben_Kingsley.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "He joined the Royal Shakespeare Company in 1967.", "cited_source": "Ben_Kingsley.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "He spent the next 15 years appearing mainly on stage.", "cited_source": "Ben_Kingsley.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "His stage productions included As You Like It, Much Ado About Nothing, Richard III, The Tempest, A Midsummer Night's Dream, Hamlet, and The Merry Wives of Windsor.", "cited_source": "Ben_Kingsley.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "He made his feature film debut in Fear Is the Key (1972).", "cited_source": "Ben_Kingsley.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "He became widely known for playing Mahatma Gandhi in Gandhi (1982).", "cited_source": "Ben_Kingsley.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "His performance in Gandhi won him the Academy Award for Best Actor.", "cited_source": "Ben_Kingsley.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "His performance in Gandhi won him the BAFTA Award for Best Actor in a Leading Role.", "cited_source": "Ben_Kingsley.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "Other notable films listed inc