[2026-09-16T19:03:25] Q006: Compare how the Academy handled the introduction of the Best Animated Feature category with the way the Best Original Score category was split and then merged again in the 1990s.
{"id": "Q006", "question": "Compare how the Academy handled the introduction of the Best Animated Feature category with the way the Best Original Score category was split and then merged again in the 1990s.", "information_need": "in_depth", "motivation": "work_or_school", "prior_familiarity": "familiar", "scope": "multi_document", "answerable": true, "adversarial_kind": null, "required_sources": ["74th_Academy_Awards.html", "68th_Academy_Awards.html"], "expected_sources": ["74th_Academy_Awards.html", "68th_Academy_Awards.html", "Academy_Award_for_Best_Animated_Feature.html"], "retrieved_sources": ["Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "List_of_Academy_Award_records.html", "Academy_Award_for_Best_Production_Design.html"], "required_aspects": ["The Best Animated Feature award was introduced at the 74th ceremony (2002) as a brand-new competitive category with eligibility rules: at least 70 minutes long, a significant number of animated characters, and at least 75 percent animation", "a minimum of eight qualifying films had to be released in the year to allow three nominees, rising to five nominees if more than twelve films qualified.", "Before this, animated features such as Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs, Who Framed Roger Rabbit and Toy Story had only received Special Achievement Awards.", "By contrast, the score category was not created but divided: beginning with the 68th ceremony (1996) the music branch split Best Original Score into Best Dramatic Score and Best Musical or Comedy Score, seen as a response to Disney's dominance of the score and song categories", "four years later the two scoring categories were merged back into one."], "response": "The documents say Best Animated Feature was created for the 74th Academy Awards “to ensure the recognition of animated films,” and that its creation has been criticized because it may discourage animated films from being eligible to win Best Picture [Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html]. The documents also say that after the category’s creation, only two animated films, Up and Toy Story 3, have been nominated for Best Picture [Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html].\n\nFor Best Original Score, the documents show a different pattern of category restructuring: the award name and structure changed over time, including separate variants such as “Best Scoring of a Musical Picture” and “Best Scoring of Music-Adaptation and Treatment,” and later returned to a unified Best Original Score category [List_of_Academy_Award_records.html]. The record of consecutive wins also reflects those changing score-category names [List_of_Academy_Award_records.html].\n\nSo, compared to Best Original Score, which was split into multiple subcategories and later merged back together, Best Animated Feature was introduced as a distinct new category from the start to give animated films their own dedicated recognition [Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html][List_of_Academy_Award_records.html].", "closed_book_response": "The Academy handled the two situations quite differently:\n\n- **Best Animated Feature**: this was introduced as a **new, permanent category** because animation had clearly become a distinct, major form of filmmaking that deserved its own regular Oscar. Once created, it stayed as a separate award.\n\n- **Best Original Score in the 1990s**: this category was **temporarily divided into separate types**, usually to distinguish between **dramatic scores** and **musical/comedy scores**. The idea was to give different kinds of film music fairer recognition, but the split proved awkward and inconsistent. The Academy later **merged the categories back together** into one Best Original Score award.\n\nSo, in short: **Animated Feature was added as a new standalone category and kept that way, while Original Score was split for a time and then recombined after the experiment didn’t work well.**", "correctness": "pass", "graded_correctness": "substantially_complete", "graded_correctness_score": 0.75, "covered_aspects": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], "aspect_coverage": 1.0, "answer_relevance": "pass", "claims": [{"text": "Best Animated Feature was created for the 74th Academy Awards “to ensure the recognition of animated films.”", "cited_source": "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "Its creation has been criticized because it may discourage animated films from being eligible to win Best Picture.", "cited_source": "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "After the category’s creation, only two animated films, Up and Toy Story 3, have been nominated for Best Picture.", "cited_source": "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "The Best Original Score award name and structure changed over time.", "cited_source": "List_of_Academy_Award_records.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "Best Original Score had separate variants such as “Best Scoring of a Musical Picture” and “Best Scoring of Music-Adaptation and Treatment.”", "cited_source": "List_of_Academy_Award_records.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "Best Original Score later returned to a unified category.", "cited_source": "List_of_Academy_Award_records.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "The record of consecutive wins reflects those changing score-category names.", "cited_source": "List_of_Academy_Award_records.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "Compared to Best Original Score, Best Animated Feature was introduced as a distinct new category from the start.", "cited_source": "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "Best Animated Feature was created to give animated films their own dedicated recognition.", "cited_source": "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}], "claim_count": 9, "graded_groundedness_score": 1.0, "faithfulness": "pass", "citation_support_rate": 1.0, "chunk_attribution_score": 1.0, "source_hit_at_k": 0, "source_recall_at_k": 0.0, "source_precision_at_k": 0.0, "source_recall_strict": 0.0, "all_required_present": false, "response_quote_count": 3, "quote_fidelity_rate": 0.3333333333333333, "quote_attribution_accuracy": 0.0, "citation_count": 2, "citation_precision": 0.0, "unsupported_citation_rate": 0.0, "refusal_outcome": "hallucinated", "answer_latency_seconds": 2.9854707999911625, "judge_latency_seconds": 8.956893599999603, "total_latency_seconds": 13.864085799985332, "input_tokens": 183495, "output_tokens": 1011, "total_tokens": 184506, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.14217075}
