[2026-09-16T19:03:36] Q019: How did the director of La La Land get his start, and what connects his college years to that film's music?
{"id": "Q019", "question": "How did the director of La La Land get his start, and what connects his college years to that film's music?", "information_need": "in_depth", "motivation": "intrinsic_learning", "prior_familiarity": "familiar", "scope": "multi_document", "answerable": true, "adversarial_kind": null, "required_sources": ["La_La_Land.html", "Damien_Chazelle.html"], "expected_sources": ["La_La_Land.html", "Damien_Chazelle.html"], "retrieved_sources": ["La_La_Land.html", "Titanic_(1997_film).html", "New_Girl.html"], "required_aspects": ["Damien Chazelle met composer Justin Hurwitz at Harvard, where they were roommates in Currier House and explored a musical concept in their senior thesis, the low-budget Guy and Madeline on a Park Bench about a Boston jazz musician.", "Both moved to Los Angeles in 2010 and continued writing what became La La Land, altering the location from Boston to Los Angeles.", "Hurwitz composed and orchestrated the songs and score for La La Land, with lyrics by Pasek and Paul except for 'Start a Fire'."], "response": "Damien Chazelle got his start by writing and developing the screenplay for *La La Land* after he had already moved to Los Angeles in 2010, and he had previously conceived the film while he was a student at Harvard University with his classmate Justin Hurwitz [La_La_Land.html]. The film’s music connects back to those college years because Chazelle and Hurwitz first explored the musical concept together at Harvard, and Hurwitz later composed the score and songs for *La La Land* [La_La_Land.html].", "closed_book_response": "Damien Chazelle got his start by making a very intense, music-centered student film while he was in college: **_Guy and Madeline on a Park Bench_**. It was his first feature and came out of his years at **Harvard**, where he studied alongside musician **Justin Hurwitz**.\n\nWhat connects his college years to **_La La Land_** is **Hurwitz** himself: Chazelle and Hurwitz were classmates at Harvard, and Hurwitz later composed the score and songs for *La La Land*. So the film’s music has a direct link back to Chazelle’s college days.", "correctness": "fail", "graded_correctness": "partial", "graded_correctness_score": 0.5, "covered_aspects": [1, 2, 3], "aspect_coverage": 1.0, "answer_relevance": "pass", "claims": [{"text": "Damien Chazelle wrote and developed the screenplay for *La La Land* after moving to Los Angeles in 2010.", "cited_source": "La_La_Land.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "Chazelle had previously conceived the film while he was a student at Harvard University with his classmate Justin Hurwitz.", "cited_source": "La_La_Land.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "Chazelle and Hurwitz first explored the musical concept together at Harvard.", "cited_source": "La_La_Land.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "Justin Hurwitz later composed the score and songs for *La La Land*.", "cited_source": "La_La_Land.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}], "claim_count": 4, "graded_groundedness_score": 1.0, "faithfulness": "pass", "citation_support_rate": 1.0, "chunk_attribution_score": 0.75, "source_hit_at_k": 1, "source_recall_at_k": 0.5, "source_precision_at_k": 0.3333333333333333, "source_recall_strict": 0.0, "all_required_present": false, "response_quote_count": 0, "quote_fidelity_rate": null, "quote_attribution_accuracy": null, "citation_count": 1, "citation_precision": 1.0, "unsupported_citation_rate": 0.0, "refusal_outcome": "n/a", "answer_latency_seconds": 1.6961503999773413, "judge_latency_seconds": 6.602113900036784, "total_latency_seconds": 10.019947599997977, "input_tokens": 269233, "output_tokens": 522, "total_tokens": 269755, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.20427375}
