[2026-09-16T19:03:46] Q042: I've heard people say Crash winning Best Picture was a bad decision — what does the record actually say about how that's been assessed since?
{"id": "Q042", "question": "I've heard people say Crash winning Best Picture was a bad decision — what does the record actually say about how that's been assessed since?", "information_need": "overview", "motivation": "personal_decision", "prior_familiarity": "familiar", "scope": "multi_document", "answerable": true, "adversarial_kind": null, "required_sources": ["78th_Academy_Awards.html", "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "Brokeback_Mountain.html"], "expected_sources": ["78th_Academy_Awards.html", "Brokeback_Mountain.html", "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html"], "retrieved_sources": ["Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "78th_Academy_Awards.html", "Brokeback_Mountain.html"], "required_aspects": ["Crash's win over Brokeback Mountain has come to be seen as one of the most notorious decisions in modern Academy history and a source of earnest bafflement from critics, with rankings by several publications calling Crash one of the worst or most controversial Best Picture winners.", "Kenneth Turan accused Academy members of homophobia and of benefitting from a non-groundbreaking choice, and after announcing the award, presenter Jack Nicholson was caught mouthing 'whoa' in apparent surprise.", "In a 2015 Hollywood Reporter poll of Academy members on controversial past decisions, Brokeback Mountain won the revote for Best Picture."], "response": "The record says Crash’s Best Picture win over Brokeback Mountain was criticized at the time and has remained controversial afterward. The 78th Academy Awards page says the decision was “widely criticized,” and that in retrospective commentary Crash’s win “has become ‘one of the most notorious [decisions] in modern Academy history’” and a source of “earnest bafflement from critics” [78th_Academy_Awards.html]. The Brokeback Mountain page likewise says that after Brokeback Mountain lost Best Picture to Crash, “some critics accused the Academy of homophobia and for making a non-groundbreaking choice” [Brokeback_Mountain.html]. It also notes that in 2015, Academy members polled by The Hollywood Reporter would have given Brokeback Mountain Best Picture over Crash [Brokeback_Mountain.html].", "closed_book_response": "If by “the record” you mean the critical and historical consensus, **Crash winning Best Picture is very often treated as one of the most controversial Best Picture outcomes in Oscar history**.\n\nWhat people usually say about it, in broad terms:\n\n- **At the time, the win was seen as a surprise and a shock** because many expected *Brokeback Mountain* to win.\n- **In hindsight, critics and awards observers have often ranked it among the weakest Best Picture winners**, especially compared with the other nominees from that year.\n- It’s frequently cited in “worst Best Picture winner” conversations, though not everyone would put it at the very bottom.\n- The common complaint is that **its reputation has not aged especially well**, while some of the other 2005 nominees are now seen as more enduring.\n\nThat said, there are a couple of important nuances:\n\n- Some people still defend it as a **well-acted, thematically ambitious ensemble drama** that resonated strongly with Academy voters at the time.\n- The negative reassessment is mostly about **its standing relative to other Best Picture winners**, not that it’s universally considered a bad film.\n\nSo the short version is: **yes, the long-term assessment has generally been harsh, and Crash is widely regarded as a controversial and often poorly aged Best Picture winner.**", "correctness": "pass", "graded_correctness": "complete", "graded_correctness_score": 1.0, "covered_aspects": [1, 2, 3], "aspect_coverage": 1.0, "answer_relevance": "pass", "claims": [{"text": "Crash’s Best Picture win over Brokeback Mountain was criticized at the time and remained controversial afterward.", "cited_source": "78th_Academy_Awards.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "The 78th Academy Awards page says the decision was “widely criticized.”", "cited_source": "78th_Academy_Awards.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "The 78th Academy Awards page says that in retrospective commentary Crash’s win “has become ‘one of the most notorious [decisions] in modern Academy history’.”", "cited_source": "78th_Academy_Awards.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "The 78th Academy Awards page says Crash’s win was a source of “earnest bafflement from critics.”", "cited_source": "78th_Academy_Awards.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "After Brokeback Mountain lost Best Picture to Crash, some critics accused the Academy of homophobia.", "cited_source": "Brokeback_Mountain.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "After Brokeback Mountain lost Best Picture to Crash, some critics said the Academy had made a non-groundbreaking choice.", "cited_source": "Brokeback_Mountain.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "In 2015, Academy members polled by The Hollywood Reporter would have given Brokeback Mountain Best Picture over Crash.", "cited_source": "Brokeback_Mountain.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}], "claim_count": 7, "graded_groundedness_score": 1.0, "faithfulness": "pass", "citation_support_rate": 1.0, "chunk_attribution_score": 1.0, "source_hit_at_k": 1, "source_recall_at_k": 1.0, "source_precision_at_k": 1.0, "source_recall_strict": 1.0, "all_required_present": true, "response_quote_count": 4, "quote_fidelity_rate": 0.5, "quote_attribution_accuracy": 0.0, "citation_count": 2, "citation_precision": 1.0, "unsupported_citation_rate": 0.0, "refusal_outcome": "n/a", "answer_latency_seconds": 2.027284799987683, "judge_latency_seconds": 5.920145700016292, "total_latency_seconds": 10.474903900001664, "input_tokens": 157328, "output_tokens": 911, "total_tokens": 158239, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.1220955}
