[2026-09-16T19:04:30] Q067: What awards did Whiplash win at Sundance when it premiered, and how does that relate to the short film of the same name?
{"id": "Q067", "question": "What awards did Whiplash win at Sundance when it premiered, and how does that relate to the short film of the same name?", "information_need": "overview", "motivation": "work_or_school", "prior_familiarity": "familiar", "scope": "multi_document", "answerable": true, "adversarial_kind": null, "required_sources": ["Whiplash_(2014_film).html", "La_La_Land.html"], "expected_sources": ["Whiplash_(2014_film).html", "La_La_Land.html", "Damien_Chazelle.html"], "retrieved_sources": ["Whiplash_(2014_film).html", "2014_Sundance_Film_Festival.html", "La_La_Land.html"], "required_aspects": ["The feature Whiplash premiered in competition at the 2014 Sundance Film Festival on January 16 as the festival's opening film and won both the Audience Award Dramatic and the Grand Jury Prize Dramatic.", "One year earlier, Chazelle's eighteen-minute short of the same name — made from fifteen pages of the feature script to attract investors — debuted at the 2013 festival and won the short film Jury Award for fiction.", "That earlier premiere later caused the Academy to classify the feature screenplay as adapted rather than original."], "response": "At its 2014 Sundance Film Festival premiere, *Whiplash* won the **Audience Award Dramatic** and the **Grand Jury Prize Dramatic** [Whiplash_(2014_film).html]. The festival page also says the opening film was *Whiplash* and that it received the **U.S. Grand Jury Prize: Dramatic** and **Audience Award: U.S. Dramatic** [2014_Sundance_Film_Festival.html].\n\nThis relates to the short film of the same name because Damien Chazelle’s **short film** version of *Whiplash* premiered at the **2013 Sundance Film Festival** and won the **short film Jury Award for fiction** [Whiplash_(2014_film).html]. The feature was later made after the short’s acclaim helped attract investors to produce the full-length version [Whiplash_(2014_film).html].", "closed_book_response": "At Sundance, **_Whiplash_** won both the **Grand Jury Prize** and the **Audience Award** in the **U.S. Dramatic** competition.\n\nIt relates to the earlier **short film of the same name** because Damien Chazelle first made **_Whiplash_** as a short, and the feature film was later developed from that short. In other words, the Sundance-winning feature is an expansion of the original short rather than a completely separate story.", "correctness": "pass", "graded_correctness": "complete", "graded_correctness_score": 1.0, "covered_aspects": [1, 2, 3], "aspect_coverage": 1.0, "answer_relevance": "pass", "claims": [{"text": "At its 2014 Sundance Film Festival premiere, Whiplash won the Audience Award Dramatic.", "cited_source": "Whiplash_(2014_film).html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "At its 2014 Sundance Film Festival premiere, Whiplash won the Grand Jury Prize Dramatic.", "cited_source": "Whiplash_(2014_film).html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "The festival page says the opening film was Whiplash.", "cited_source": "2014_Sundance_Film_Festival.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "The festival page says Whiplash received the U.S. Grand Jury Prize: Dramatic.", "cited_source": "2014_Sundance_Film_Festival.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "The festival page says Whiplash received the Audience Award: U.S. Dramatic.", "cited_source": "2014_Sundance_Film_Festival.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "Damien Chazelle’s short film version of Whiplash premiered at the 2013 Sundance Film Festival.", "cited_source": "Whiplash_(2014_film).html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "Damien Chazelle’s short film version of Whiplash won the short film Jury Award for fiction.", "cited_source": "Whiplash_(2014_film).html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "The feature was later made after the short’s acclaim helped attract investors to produce the full-length version.", "cited_source": "Whiplash_(2014_film).html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "At Sundance, Whiplash won both the Grand Jury Prize and the Audience Award in the U.S. Dramatic competition.", "cited_source": null, "grounded": true, "citation_supported": null, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "Whiplash relates to the earlier short film of the same name.", "cited_source": null, "grounded": true, "citation_supported": null, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "Damien Chazelle first made Whiplash as a short.", "cited_source": null, "grounded": true, "citation_supported": null, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "The feature film was later developed from that short.", "cited_source": null, "grounded": true, "citation_supported": null, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "The Sundance-winning feature is an expansion of the original short rather than a completely separate story.", "cited_source": null, "grounded": false, "citation_supported": null, "attributable_to_retrieval": null}], "claim_count": 13, "graded_groundedness_score": 0.9230769230769231, "faithfulness": "fail", "citation_support_rate": 1.0, "chunk_attribution_score": 0.16666666666666666, "source_hit_at_k": 1, "source_recall_at_k": 1.0, "source_precision_at_k": 0.6666666666666666, "source_recall_strict": 1.0, "all_required_present": true, "response_quote_count": 0, "quote_fidelity_rate": null, "quote_attribution_accuracy": null, "citation_count": 2, "citation_precision": 0.5, "unsupported_citation_rate": 0.0, "refusal_outcome": "n/a", "answer_latency_seconds": 2.536471100000199, "judge_latency_seconds": 7.5523938999685925, "total_latency_seconds": 11.382337399962125, "i