{"id": "Q080", "question": "Tell me about Anthony Minghella — what did he win and what happened at the Oscars after his death?", "information_need": "overview", "motivation": "intrinsic_learning", "prior_familiarity": "unfamiliar", "scope": "multi_document", "answerable": true, "adversarial_kind": null, "required_sources": ["Anthony_Minghella.html", "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html"], "expected_sources": ["Anthony_Minghella.html", "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html"], "retrieved_sources": ["David_Fincher.html", "Anthony_Minghella.html", "Cillian_Murphy.html"], "required_aspects": ["Anthony Minghella (1954–2008) was a British playwright and filmmaker who directed Truly, Madly, Deeply, The English Patient, The Talented Mr.", "Ripley and Cold Mountain.", "He won the Academy Award for Best Director for The English Patient, and received three further nominations: Best Adapted Screenplay for both The English Patient and The Talented Mr.", "Ripley, and, posthumously, Best Picture for The Reader (2008) as a producer.", "The Academy made an exception to its normal three-producer limit for Best Picture so that Minghella and Sydney Pollack could be posthumously included among the four producers nominated for The Reader."], "response": "Anthony Minghella was a British playwright and filmmaker who “received the Academy Award for Best Director for The English Patient.” [Anthony_Minghella.html] He also had three more Academy Award nominations, including Best Adapted Screenplay for *The English Patient* and *The Talented Mr. Ripley*, and a posthumous Best Picture nomination for *The Reader* as a producer. [Anthony_Minghella.html]\n\nThe documents do not say what specifically happened at the Oscars after his death beyond that posthumous nomination. [Anthony_Minghella.html]", "closed_book_response": "Anthony Minghella was a British film director, screenwriter, and producer, best known for films like *The English Patient*, *Truly, Madly, Deeply*, and *The Talented Mr. Ripley*.\n